# Implementation Plan: Firebase Authentication

To enable **Fluid Sync** (Cross-Device & Cloud Access), we need to secure the Marketing Dashboard and Nucleus Server using Firebase Authentication.

## Goal
Replace open/local access with Identity-Aware access.
- **Frontend**: Users log in with Google/Email to access the Dashboard.
- **Backend**: API verifies ID tokens before processing requests.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Firebase Project Setup Required**
> You will need a Firebase Project. 
> 1. Go to [console.firebase.google.com](https://console.firebase.google.com)
> 2. Create/Select a project.
> 3. Enable **Authentication** (Google Provider or Email/Password).
> 4. Copy the **Web App Config** for [firebase_config.js](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/firebase_config.js).
> 5. Generate a **Service Account Key** (`service_account.json`) for the backend.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Setup & Configuration
#### [NEW] [tools/marketing-dashboard/firebase_config.js](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/firebase_config.js)
- Placeholder file for Firebase Web Config.
- **Action**: User populates this.

#### [NEW] [secret/service_account.json](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/secret/service_account.json) (GitIgnored)
- Path for the backend credential.

### 2. Frontend (Marketing Dashboard)
#### [MODIFY] [tools/marketing-dashboard/index.html](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/index.html)
- Import Firebase SDK (v9/v10 compat or CDN).
- Add `Login` / `Logout` buttons.
### [Authentication System]

#### [NEW] [firebase_config.js](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/firebase_config.js)
- Placeholder for Firebase Web App configuration.
- **ACTION REQUIRED**: User must populate this file.

#### [NEW] [service_account.json](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/secret/service_account.json)
- **ACTION REQUIRED**: User must download this key from Firebase Console -> Project Settings -> Service Accounts and place it here.
- Added to [.gitignore](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/.gitignore) to prevent leaks.

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/index.html)
- Added Firebase SDKs (Auth, App).
- Added [login()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/index.html#249-253) / [logout()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/index.html#254-257) UI.
- Added `Authorization: Bearer <token>` to all API calls.
- UI hides "Agent Portal" until logged in.

#### [MODIFY] [server.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/server.py)
- Integrated `firebase_admin` SDK.
- Added [verify_token()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/server.py#81-99) middleware.
- Returns `401 Unauthorized` if token is invalid.
- Falls back to "Unsecured Dev Mode" if `service_account.json` is missing.

